  "name": "VGKC (VOLTAGE GATED POTASSIUM CHANNEL) ANTIBODY-CSF",
  "code": "1336",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li>Auto Immune reactivity are not by themselves diagnostic and must be correlated with other laboratory<br>and clinical findings.</li>\n<li>Test conducted on undiluted CSF.</li>\n<li>Antigen substrate - transfected cells of EU-90.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong> In ~80% cases of VGKC antibody- associated syndromes (autoimmune voltage- gated potassium<br>channelopathies) target antigens are LG1 and CASPR2. Autoantibodies against LGI1 are detected usually in<br>limbic encephalitis (89 - 100%). Autoantibosies against CASPR2 are detected in neuromyopathy and Morvan&rsquo;s<br>syndrome (~53%), limbic encephalitis (~37%) and isolated epilepsy (~11%).</p>",
